          hasPlaceholders: false,
        },
        rules: {
          objective: "Be the first to shed all cards. When you play your last card, you must yell 'Mao!'.",
          gameplay: "Play proceeds clockwise from the dealer's left. On your turn, play one card that matches the rank or suit of the top card on the play pile, or draw one card from the stock if you cannot play. Breaking a rule incurs a penalty card. First to empty their hand and call 'Mao' (or 'game over') wins. Rules vary by group and are often learned by trial and error.",
          keyRules: [
            'Match the top card on the play pile by rank or suit; or draw one from stock if unable.',
            'Call Mao or game over when playing your last card.',
            'One penalty card per rule breach; the person giving it states what was wrong without explaining the rule.',
            'Rules vary by group and are learned by observation and trial and error.',
          ],
          hasPlaceholders: false,
        },
        strategy: {
          basic: "Don't be the first to act! Watch the veterans. If they say 'Have a nice Day' every time they play a 7, YOU should say it too. Most of Mao is pattern recognition.",
          intermediate: "The 'Chairman' Trap: If you are the Chairman, use your power to confuse new players. Give penalties for 'Failure to be Awesome' or 'Breathing too loudly'. This forces players to think outside the literal mechanics of the cards.",
          advanced: "Rule-Stacking: If you win, create a rule that is triggered by a common action. For example, 'Every time a Red 4 is played, the person who played it must stand up.' Combine this with existing rules to create complex sequences of required actions.",
          tips: [
            "Keep a straight face. If you laugh at a penalty, you might get another penalty for 'Illegal Joy'.",
            "If you are stuck, call a 'Point of Order'. It's the only safe time to observe the table without cards in hand.",
          ],
          hasPlaceholders: false,
        },
